==Finnish==
[[File:Riihilampi 2019.jpg|thumb]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*lampi}}, probably from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*lëmpe}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-p}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[pond]] {{gloss|inland body of standing water, usually natural, that is smaller than a lake}}

====Usage notes====
* A man-made pond is usually called {{m|fi|allas}} or {{m|fi|tekoallas}} in Finnish.

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-ovi|la|mp|mm|a}}
In many dialects, the word has traditionally been inflected as an ''i''-stem (genitive {{m|fi||lammin}}), and this form is reflected in some place names and surnames. However, only the above ''e''-stem declension is accepted in Standard Finnish.
{{fi-decl-risti|la|mp|mm|a}}

